From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:20:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(hud): honor death message visibility

Keep the translated death reason in session storage and apply
showDeathMessages when sending the death screen. Share this policy between
DeathInfo and actor-death handling so either packet order hides only the
reason. Refresh a dead player when the rule changes, including restoring
the retained reason when it is enabled again.

Bedrock 1.26.60.5, protocol 2225, evaluates this rule in its active OreUI
PlayerDeathInfoQuery as well as its classic death controller. Eight
original-executable query controls select an empty string unless the world,
player and enabled rule are all present. Executable SHA-256:
988f6a61403b4381aa41e6c66d64cce441b14e561a9b10f647c2758ef3f2672a.

Packet regressions cover both arrival orders, alive-player admission,
retained text, live rule changes and repeated unchanged rules. This fixes
reason projection; the OreUI screen layout and lifecycle remain separate
work.
